PRIVACY_POLICY_HTML = r'''<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>SubSathi Privacy Policy</title><style>body{font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:850px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#142b22}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}a{color:#087750}.note{padding:14px;border-radius:12px;background:#e7f8ef}</style></head><body>
<h1>SubSathi Privacy Policy</h1><p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 12 October 2026</p>
<p>SubSathi helps you organise subscriptions and recurring expenses. This policy describes the intended handling for the SubSathi API and Gmail subscription-discovery feature. Publish a reviewed copy at your verified public domain before public launch.</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Gmail access is optional.</strong> SubSathi never asks for your Google password. Google sign-in and Gmail read access start only after you select Connect Gmail and approve Google's consent screen.</div>
<h2>Information processed</h2><ul><li>Google account identifier, verified email and display name to identify the account.</li><li>OAuth access and refresh credentials, encrypted on the server so the service can access Gmail after consent and refresh authorised access.</li><li>Billing-related email metadata extracted by the scanner, such as service name, price, billing cycle and an explicitly stated renewal date.</li><li>Technical timestamps and scan results needed to operate the service and avoid duplicate imports.</li></ul>
<h2>Gmail use</h2><p>The scanner uses the Gmail API to search for billing-related messages. Email bodies are processed in memory for metadata extraction and are not persisted as full messages by the scanner. Detected values can be incomplete or wrong; users should review them before relying on reminders. The API stores extracted subscription candidates and a small amount of metadata, not full email bodies or complete subjects.</p>
<h2>Use and sharing</h2><p>Information is used to provide subscription discovery, account security, duplicate detection and the requested product features. SubSathi must not sell Gmail contents or use email contents for advertising. Hosting and security providers may process data solely to provide the service. Any future affiliate or partner revenue must be disclosed and must not determine private inbox scans.</p>
<h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>Gmail credentials and extracted candidates are retained while the account remains connected, unless deleted earlier. Use Disconnect Gmail to remove server-stored credentials and cached scan candidates. Use account deletion to delete the server account and associated connected-service data. Imported subscription entries stored locally on an Android device must be deleted separately in the app.</p>
<h2>Security</h2><p>OAuth credentials are encrypted at rest using an application-managed encryption key. Production deployment must use HTTPS, strong secrets, access controls, a private database, dependency updates, backups with retention controls and incident response procedures. Do not publish until these controls and Google's applicable OAuth verification/security assessment requirements have been reviewed.</p>
<h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may decline Gmail access and use local/manual tracking. You can disconnect Gmail, delete your server account and clear local entries independently. To ask a privacy question, configure a monitored support email in the production release and add it here before public launch.</p>
<h2>Scope and contact</h2><p>This policy is a project draft, not legal advice. The publisher must add its legal business name, working contact details, final retention periods, data processor list and jurisdiction-specific terms before production release.</p>
</body></html>'''

TERMS_HTML = r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>SubSathi Terms</title><style>body{font:16px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:850px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;color:#142b22}</style></head><body><h1>SubSathi Terms of Use</h1><p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 12 October 2026</p><p>SubSathi is a subscription-organising tool. Detected information is provided for convenience and can be incomplete, delayed or incorrect. Always confirm price, renewal date and cancellation terms with the provider.</p><p>SubSathi does not process subscription renewals or cancel a provider plan unless a specific authorised integration is built and clearly disclosed. Opening an official manage link does not itself change a subscription.</p><p>Keep your device secure and only connect accounts you control. Do not use the service to access another person's inbox without permission. The public publisher must add its legal identity, contact email, payment/refund terms and applicable-law provisions before accepting paying customers.</p></body></html>'''